          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Cellular homology is a very efficient tool for computing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+groups"} homology groups
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            which are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complexes"} CW complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+singular+homology"} relative singular homology
            of their
            = succeed "-decomposition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complex"} cell complex
            = succeed "-computations." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+continuous+function"} degree
          %p
            Hence cellular homology uses the combinatorial structure of a CW-complex to define, first a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of
            %em celluar chains
            and then the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            %em cellular homology
            of a CW-complex is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            as a topological space, and hence provides an efficient method for computing the latter.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#cwcomplex CW-Complex
          %p
            For definiteness and to fix notation which we need in the following, we recall the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CellularHomology"} below
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                for the standard
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^n \in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                for the standard
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \hookrightarrow D^{n+1}
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                that includes the
                = succeed "-sphere" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
                of the
                = succeed "-disk." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
          %p
            Write furthermore
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} \coloneqq \emptyset
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            topological space and think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} \to D^0 \simeq *
            as the boundary inclusion of the (-1)-sphere into the 0-disk, which is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
          #CWComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %p
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n}
              obtained from
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-complex" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CW
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CW
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n-1}
                  of dimension
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              %li
                %p
                  an index set
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Cell
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Set
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cell(X)_n \in Set
              %li
                %p
                  a set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
                  (the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %strong attaching maps
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi Cell
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ f_i \colon S^{n-1} \to X_{n-1}\}_{i \in Cell(X)_n}
            %p
              as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Cell
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Cell
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \simeq \coprod_{j \in Cell(X)_n} D^n \coprod_{j \in Cell(X)_n S^{n-1}} X_n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi Cell
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi n
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi Cell
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi n
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\coprod_{j \in Cell(X)_{n}} S^{n-1} &amp;\stackrel{(f_j)}{\to}&amp; X_{n-1}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\coprod_{j \in Cell(X)_{n}} D^{n} &amp;\to&amp; X_{n}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By this construction an
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+topological+space"} filtered topological space
              with filter inclusion maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\emptyset \hookrightarrow X_0 \hookrightarrow X_1 \hookrightarrow \cdots \hookrightarrow X_{n-1} \hookrightarrow X_n
            %p the right vertical morphisms in these pushout diagrams.
            %p
              A general
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              given as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} sequential colimit
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower"} tower
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              each of whose morphisms is such a filter inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\emptyset \hookrightarrow X_0 \hookrightarrow X_1 \hookrightarrow \cdots \hookrightarrow X
                    \\,.
          %p
            For the following a CW-complex is all this data: the chosen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+topological+space"} filtering
            with the chosen attaching maps.
          %h3#CellularHomology Cellular homology
          %p
            We define “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"}> ordinary
            ” cellular homology with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            is immediate.
          #CellularChainComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWComplex"}
              %strong cellular chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                      %mi CW
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet^{CW}(X) \in Ch_\bullet
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              such that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chains"} chains
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+singular+homology"} relative singular homology
                  group of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \hookrightarrow X
                  relative to
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n-1} \hookrightarrow X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                          %mi CW
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H_n^{CW}(X) \coloneqq H_n(X_n, X_{n-1})
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mi CW
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mi CW
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                          %mi CW
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^{CW}_{n+1} \colon H_{n+1}^{CW}(X) \to H_n^{CW}(X)
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi n
                          %mi CW
